# Store mutex init data race

**DONE.** Closed before these files carried a status word. The `.done`
suffix is the record; this line is that same answer in the second place
the check reads, and no new judgement.

Review finding 11. store.cpp register_/lookup do check-then-assign on
void* lock_ unsynchronized; two concurrent pool adds is C++ UB and can
create two mutexes over one set.

Fix: initialize the mutex in the Store constructor or use std::once_flag.

## Done 2026-08-25

Store now has a declared constructor that creates the mutex, so no
call site ever sees a null pointer. lookup drops its null branch with
it. std::once_flag was the alternative; a constructor is simpler and
the header stays free of <mutex> either way.
